before:
Worked example:

```javascript
function appendNote(notes,note) {
  return [...notes,{...note}];
}
console.log(appendNote([{"id":1,"title":"Moon"}], {"id":2,"title":"Sea"}));
```
The returned value is [{"id":1,"title":"Moon"},{"id":2,"title":"Sea"}].

after:
```javascript
function appendNote(notes,note) {
  return [...notes,{...note}];
}
console.log(appendNote([{"id":1,"title":"Moon"}], {"id":2,"title":"Sea"}));
```
The result contains Moon first and Sea second. The earlier note stays unchanged, and the added note keeps its supplied ID and title.
